<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong unit trust gross sales double in July.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong unit trust gross sales double in July.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Investment Funds Association (HKIFA) said on Monday the local unit trust industry registered gross sales of US$491.62 million in July versus US$245.13 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>US$140.83 million, or about 28.7 percent, was new money, compared to US$14 million in July 1995, it said.</p>
<p>HKIFA chairman Andrew Lo said the pickup in sales was due to recovery of U.S. equity and bond markets.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
